      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_kelberi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Cichla kelberi is a species that was only recognized in 2006. It is available only in very limited numbers.</p><p>The species is distinguished from its closest relative, C. monoculus, by the presence of light spots in the pelvic fins, the anal fin and the lower lobe of the caudal fin in adults.</p><p>Cichla kelberi attains a total length of about 30 cm, which makes it one of the smallest members of the genus.</p>"
    }
